      "side": 1,
      "message": "@smostafa@google.com\n\n`SID_DONT_CARE` is just a macro (`#define SID_DONT_CARE (-1)`) in `pviommu-host.h`, but it\u0027s used as `u32` in `arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/iommu/pviommu-host.c`.\n\n`pkvm_pviommu_route()` takes `vsid` as `u32`, so I thought that `u32` is bit more correct although knowing that `vsid` is `u32` involves too much internal details.\n\nSo my follow-up questions are:\n\n  - Would it be better to change `SID_DONT_CARE` to `u64::MAX`?\n  - Should I change `vsid` param to `Option\u003cu32\u003e` or validate given `vsid` is in valid `u32` range?",
      "parentUuid": "0dd1dfb2_20fad144",
